  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933758/assets/6ba976f250811d1ba3109f4aecbfdb2a4de4ee86300fa867e80e2087aa21601f.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=sin\u2061x.$\n\n- Then, reflect it in the $x$-axis to give $y=-sin\u2061x.$\n\n- Finally, stretch it parallel to the $y$-axis by a stretch factor of $\\frac{7}{4}$ to give $y=-\\frac{7}{4}sin\u2061x.$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=-\\frac{7}{4}sin\u2061x.$",
